    description: "Corrective per-language pass surfaced by the 2026-07-19 INV-fahub validation bakeoff. The fleet gate (defer_bare_method_call, merged across 11 analyzers) gates each analyzer BARE-IDENTIFIER free-call resolver path, but INV-fahub's funnel is UNTYPED-RECEIVER method calls (x.method() where x's type is unresolvable), which for Go/Rust resolve via a SEPARATE method/selector path never gated; D FREE-FORM stdlib calls (writeln(x)->internal method) are a third ungated path (D excluded from the fleet PR). Real-repro evidence (scratchpad/inv-fahub/{funnel,fleet_magnet}.py + *.json): Scala(docspell) CLEAN 0 magnets; Swift(vernissage) 6 candidate magnets; Go(caddy) 41 magnets/666 binds gate-fired-1 (Dispenser.Val<-53 = d.Val() @0.85 call_construct=method); Rust(ripgrep) 23 magnets; D(dub) 9 free-form (writeln<-70/to<-33/execute<-15). TASK: per fleet language find where untyped-receiver method calls (and D free-form) resolve, gate that path via defer_bare_method_call (like Scala/Swift WI-bihit/votar receiver-gating, which is why they are clean), re-validate on real repos, flip INV-fahub. Also confirm the Swift 6 candidates (legit typed-receiver vs real) + validate csharp/php/cpp/objc/lua."  # 9ca7
